    bottomLine:
      "A sensible pick if you're sealing your garage floor alongside a basement or walkway in the same weekend and want one product that handles all three reasonably well.",
    description:
      "KILZ Concrete & Masonry Sealer is not engineered specifically for garage floors the way the Foundation Armor and Rust-Oleum products on this list are — it is a general-purpose concrete and masonry sealer that happens to work acceptably well in a garage, and we included it here because that general-purpose flexibility is genuinely useful for a certain kind of project. If you are tackling your garage floor at the same time as a basement slab, an exterior walkway, or a porch, buying one capable multi-surface sealer instead of three specialized products can simplify the shopping list and reduce leftover partial cans sitting on a shelf. In our garage-specific testing, KILZ performed in the middle of the pack: dust reduction after a single coat was modest, roughly comparable to the Quikrete budget option, and improved meaningfully once we applied the manufacturer-recommended second coat, at which point performance approached that of the Eagle EU1. Stain resistance followed the same pattern — a single coat offered only mild protection against oil and gas contact, but two coats brought it into a respectable middle tier, wiping clean fluids that had sat for five to ten minutes without staining. The extra coat does mean this is a two-day project rather than the one-coat, same-day application most of the other sealers on this list allow, since manufacturer guidance calls for four hours of dry time between coats and the second coat still needs to cure before vehicle traffic. One genuine advantage: because it is formulated as a versatile base sealer rather than a specialty finish, it plays nicely as a substrate if you later decide to upgrade to paint or a decorative topcoat, which is not something every acrylic garage sealer guarantees. For a homeowner sealing multiple concrete surfaces around the property in one weekend push, the convenience of one capable product outweighs the modest performance gap versus the garage-specialized options above.",
